# s5_embed_chunk: private embedding one-hot matmul in 16 vocabulary chunks.
#
# table      p_census_owner_s4 (rss 2,332,684 vs peak 2,336,656 kB, 0.17%; deduplicated by data_ptr):
#              534.5 MB  n=3   (28996, 768)      the embedding table
#              237.5 MB  n=8   (1, 128, 28996)   the one-hot intermediates
#              178.2 MB  n=1   (22268928,)       28996 x 768 flat
#              --------
#              950.2 MB = 41.5% of the peak, and every row of it is embedding-shaped.
# phase      forward pass is a flat plateau:
#              run1   t+0s 2016 MB   t+30s 2008   t+70s 2077
#              run2   t+0s 2192      t+30s 2232   t+75s 2232
#            nothing retained past last use (s5_graph_clear_values 0.02%, also with pinned allocator);
#            the embedding must shrink.
# donor      SHAFT-GPU s2_embed_chunk (impl/embed_chunk_gpu.py; VRAM 2,406,400 -> 1,546,240 kB); port with
#            malloc_trim instead of device handling. N=16 = donor value (campaign parameter).
# cost       paid (per-chunk triples and PRZS masks: same bytes, more envelopes); free levers exhausted
#            (all 21 modules measured).
# phase B    different random tape changes the fixed-point output; transcript on these runs and
#            equiv_embed_chunk against this port.
# expected   -400 to -700 MB on 2,289,520 kB (-17% to -30%); spread 9.35%.
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16"
